        {
          "say": "For an image two hundred twenty-four pixels wide and high, sixteen-pixel patches produce a fourteen-by-fourteen grid. Halving patch width doubles the number along each axis. Predict the change in total patches before the smaller cells appear. Both axes contribute to the increase.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 17.631999999999998,
          "duration": 17.232,
          "until": 18.432
        },
        {
          "say": "The token count quadruples. Dense attention compares every query with every key, so its patch-to-patch pair count grows sixteenfold. That ratio describes pairwise work under these encoder choices. Other operations and implementation details still contribute to the model's actual runtime.",
